      "value": "<p>The single moon of the ocean world below, and the reason its tides are as violent as they are. Ice-covered, fractured, with a sounded ocean and no landing yet attempted. It hangs low and enormous over the flats at every meeting the survey has attended, which is presumably not a coincidence, although nobody has been able to ask.</p>",
